# ThunderBun coding rules

## Vanilla TypeScript — no frameworks
- No React, Vue, Svelte, or dapp-kit
- All UI built with `innerHTML`, `document.createElement`, and event listeners
- Sections export a single `renderX(container: HTMLElement): void` function

## CSS — vanilla only
- Use design tokens: `var(--space-N)`, `var(--accent)`, `var(--surface-N)`, `var(--text-muted)`
- No Tailwind, no CSS-in-JS
- Component-scoped styles injected via `<style>` tag if needed

## zkproof-pipeline.ts — composability rules
- Every pipeline step must be an exported async function accepting a typed config object
- Never hardcode network URLs, object IDs, or token types inside step functions
- All secrets (keys, wallets) are passed in — never read from global state inside lib/
- `ZkProofConfig` must be the single source of truth; presets must cover all use cases

## Move (Sui 2024.beta edition)
- Use method syntax: `v.length()`, `v.borrow(i)`, `v.push_back(x)` — NOT `vector::length(v)`
- Use `std::hash` for SHA-256, NOT `sui::hash`
- `#[expected_failure(abort_code = N)]` uses integer literals, not cross-module constants
- One responsibility per module; cross-module calls are fine within the same package
- Suppress only justified lints: `#[allow(lint(self_transfer))]` on convenience wrappers
- Remove the `[dependencies]` section from Move.toml if on edition 2024.beta — MoveStdlib is auto-injected

## Environment variables
- All configurable values go in `.env` as `VITE_*` and are accessed via `import.meta.env`
- `contractFromEnv()` in `zkproof-pipeline.ts` is the canonical way to read contract IDs
- Never commit `.env` files with real keys

## Adding a new template section
1. `templates/sui-twa/src/sections/mysection.ts` → export `renderMySection`
2. Register in `main.ts`: `SectionId`, `NAV`, and `RENDERERS`

## Adding a new pipeline step
1. Add config type + add field to `ZkProofConfig`
2. Export the step function from `zkproof-pipeline.ts`
3. Insert into `runPipeline()` with a progress callback
4. Update `FULL_CONFIG`, `DEV_CONFIG`, `VERIFY_ONLY_CONFIG`
5. Add toggle to `zkproof.ts` options grid using `optionToggle()`
